keywords:
  - Grundy domination number
  - dominating sequence
  - strong product
  - counterexample
  - circular clique
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  The strong product of the octahedron with a graph H on 21 vertices of Grundy domination number 10
  has Grundy domination number at least 21. This disproves the conjecture of Brešar, Bujtás,
  Gologranc, Klavžar, Košmrlj, Patkós, Tuza and Vizer that the Grundy domination number is
  multiplicative on strong products. The upper bound for H is certified in Lean 4.
